Task 10:
///Lab: URL-based access control can be circumvented///

"X-Original-URL header." thats a huge clue..After a lot of try i did this: send the GET / request to repeater. And add a line to the end: X-Original-Url: /admin
If you send this, the response will be the admin panel, but u cant do anything here, but you have a url to delete carlos which is: /admin/delete?username=carlos
So my first try was copy this instead of the /admin...and i got a bad request missing parameter 'username'. This means the back-end server cant see my username parameter...so the solution is we are going to 
separate our url to two parts...Because the back-end is searching my parameters at the / route. so we will give him here. So the front-end will think that we ask the front page with some parameter, while the backend 
call the X-Original-Url funcion which is deleting...
So our request will look like this:
GET /?username=carlos HTTP/2
Host: 0a8a007e0352fbe081927a3400d400cb.web-security-academy.net
....
....
Referer: https://0a8a007e0352fbe081927a3400d400cb.web-security-academy.net/login
Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate, br
Priority: u=0, i
X-Original-Url: /admin/delete

